MID_LGV_1_M03_Kai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Kai_m01_001: I just fight the way I was taught, but everyone\nalways seems surprised by the style.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Kai_m01_002: My dad taught me everything I know, but I guess\nthe moves are pretty darn distinctive.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Kai_m01_003: My dad plays dumb, but I'm starting to figure out\nthat his life used to be pretty interesting.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Kai_m01: <BLN>My dad plays dumb, but...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Bel_m01_001: The exhibition match was a humbling reminder that\neven I am not unbeatable.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Bel_m01_002: What really vexes me is that I have no clue where\nthis Cruaidín person came from.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Bel_m01: <BLN>I learned a hard lesson.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Dit_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Dit_m01_001: I scent them... So many in Dagda are possessed of \ngreat strength.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Dit_m01_002: If only I could duel them here and now, but I suppose\nI must wait for the games to bring us together.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Dit_m01_003: Yes, I must be patient and wait for our day to dance.\nYet how I thirst for it.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Dit_m01: <BLN>How I thirst...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Tal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Tal_m01_001: Dagsion is quite the spectacle, isn't it? The people,\nthe culture. You'll find no shortage of wonder here.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Tal_m01_002: Haha! Don't get me wrong, folks around here can be\na little... Well, let's say "quirky."
MID_LGV_1_M03_Tal_m01_003: Lucky for me, that's just the kind of people I like to\nhire! Who knows who I'll meet next.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Tal_m01: <BLN>The capital, in all its glory.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Seo_m01_001: Saramis and the Dagdan Empire may appear to be\non good terms at the moment.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Seo_m01_002: But the fall of Damascar will always cast a pall over\nour shared history.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Seo_m01_003: I find it difficult to extend my full trust to the people\nof Dagsion.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Seo_m01: <BLN>Our history is a fraught one.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Led_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Led_Buc_m01_001: Who could have guessed my journey would take\nme here, to the imperial capital?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Led_Buc_m01_002: Dagsion. A perfect stage for the grand finale.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Led_Buc_m01_003: Right.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Led_Buc_m01_004: Come on! Wipe off the sour expression. You should\nbe glad I'm in a good mood.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Led_m01: <BLN>What better stage than this?
MID_LGA_1_M03_Buc_m01: <BLN>...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Anh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Anh_m01_001: As I expected, the temples possess extraordinary\npower in the Dagdan Empire.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Anh_m01_002: But I don't have time to worry about it. I've got a\nmission to complete.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Anh_m01: <BLN>I've got a mission.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Tia_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Tia_Pet_m01_001: Whenever we play hide-and-seek, you always find\nme in no time at all.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Tia_Pet_m01_002: I always thought you found me easy because Ribeira\nwas so small, but you do it in Dagsion too!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Tia_Pet_m01_003: Sorry, but no matter where we play, you're just as\neasy to read.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Tia_m01: <BLN>Hee hee!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Pet_m01: <BLN>Every time...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Hur_m01_001: All kinds of people show up for events like the\nHeroic Games.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Hur_m01_002: I worry about pleasing the nobles, and I get scared\nof folks who seem like ex-criminals.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Hur_m01_003: But just as I'm thinking that's all there is to life,\na bunch of cute kids show up!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Hur_m01: <BLN>All kinds of people...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Max_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Max_Gol_m01_001: I was sure the qualifiers for the Heroic Games would\nbe full o' wimps.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Max_Gol_m01_002: Turns out some of 'em have real backbone!\nTrust me, Jester. You'd like watching 'em!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Max_Gol_m01_003: Is that so? Not just a bunch of pathetic pups\ndancin' to the gods' whims?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Max_Gol_m01_004: Well then! Guess I'd better pay attention, hehehe.\nHope some of 'em are worth slicing up!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Max_m01: <BLN>Is that so, eh?
MID_LGA_1_M03_Gol_m01: <BLN>They got backbone!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Gat_m01_001: I just remembered I'm starting to run low on my\ntea powder.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Gat_m01_002: I should go to my usual store and pick some up.\nIt often has items from the east.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Gat_m01_003: And an impressive selection of furnishings as well.\nThe shop owner certainly has taste.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Gat_m01: <BLN>I'm running low...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Dan_m01_001: That fighter Cruaidín was a true paragon of battle!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Dan_m01_002: Certainly, skilled enough to take part in the starting\nexhibition. I'm just surprised he's so unknown!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Dan_m01_003: The White-Maned Demon is known to all. And the\ntemples were hiding a man even he could not defeat?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Dan_m01_004: I say it is a disgrace to keep such talent concealed.\nAs a director, I would have put him center stage!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Dan_m01: <BLN>A true revelation!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Fab_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Fab_Esm_m01_001: The imperial capital, Dagsion. A noisome and noisy\ncity, thronged with beasts.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Fab_Esm_m01_002: Didn't you come here to preach to the people? So if\nthere are a lot of people...isn't that good for you?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Fab_Esm_m01_003: What would make you think that you may lecture\nme? My every thought pertains to my mission. 
MID_LGV_1_M03_Fab_Esm_m01_004: Me? You're the one who's lecturing. I guess you don't\nhear yourself.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Fab_m01: <BLN>So unpleasant, this city.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Esm_m01: <BLN>What was that?!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Urs_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Urs_Lou_m01_001: Talimun says he doesn't like blood, but he went and\nentered the Heroic Games anyway!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Urs_Lou_m01_002: I suspect he wants to see the contestants in person.\nTo size them up properly and see their weaponry.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Urs_Lou_m01_003: Huh, makes sense. Who knows, maybe he'll hire one\nof them or, at the very least, buy their stuff off them.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Urs_Lou_m01_004: I'd also wager he's interested in what they'll wish for.\nHe's always been fascinated by desire and passion.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Urs_m01: <BLN>That's just the way he is.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Lou_m01: <BLN>What's Talimun thinking?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sim_m01_001: Even if the boss hadn't woken up, I probably\nwould've ended up in the Heroic Games anyway.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sim_m01_002: Don't have any fancy wishes of my own, but I'm sure\nthere's plenty of fighters who would've hired me.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sim_m01_003: Ask any mercenary and they'll tell you the same.\nAll we're good for is smashing people.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Sim_m01: <BLN>Woulda been here either way...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Fia_m01_001: Talimun...he's just so wonderful...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Fia_m01_002: If it were his will, I would do anything he asked...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Fia_m01_003: Wait... N-no... I couldn't do anything too untoward,\ncould I?
MID_LGA_1_M03_Fia_m01: <BLN>For Talimun, I'd...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Die_Orh_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Die_Orh_m01_001: I find nearly every single thing outside of the temples\nso exciting! Diego, aren't you keen to explore?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Die_Orh_m01_002: I just wish you weren't so keen to do that. That'll\nmake it much harder for me to guard you.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Die_Orh_m01_003: But everything's so exciting and new—everywhere\nI look in Dagsion!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Die_Orh_m01_004: Well, if you insist... I'll just work twice as hard to\nmake sure you're safe.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Die_m01: <BLN>Only if you insist.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Orh_m01: <BLN>Excited to explore?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Lor_m01_001: I swear that I won't get into scraps all over this city.\nI know it'd be bad for our temple.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Lor_m01_002: I don't want to upset the priest lady either. She's\nway too nice.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Lor_m01: <BLN>The priest lady...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Set_m01_001: There are few Crests that appear in the bloodlines\nof this empire's many houses—or in their warriors.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Set_m01_002: What a different culture than in Fódlan, where\nhaving a Crest determines one's status and position.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Set_m01: <BLN>A different culture altogether...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Nin_m01_001: Might Credna have gone somewhere? And if so,\nwhere? He didn't join the opening ceremony.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Nin_m01_002: He seemed fine, the last time I saw him. He told\nme a story—a very long story.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Nin_m01_003: What is it he said? "I appreciate that you listen to me\nblather on about blacksmithing." Yes, that's it.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Nin_m01_004: I enjoyed the experience of that discussion. I hope to\nbe in his company again soon.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Nin_m01: <BLN>Where has he gone?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Bon_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Bon_Tob_m01_001: Tobias, I have received reports of you getting drunk\nat the taverns again.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Bon_Tob_m01_002: Yeah, well, the stuff back home is great, but the\nhooch here in the capital's pretty tasty too!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Bon_Tob_m01_003: Can you blame me if I shared a cask or two with the\nyoung folks at the bar? Baw haw haw!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Bon_Tob_m01_004: This is unbecoming of a Saraminian commander.\nAt least the locals have not lodged any complaints...
MID_LGA_1_M03_Bon_m01: <BLN>You are incorrigible.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Tob_m01: <BLN>Baw haw haw!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Lil_m01_001: There's a real hunger in the eyes of a lot of these\nfolks signed up for the games.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Lil_m01_002: Guess the offer of a wish can get people to do\nanything. But me, I'll work as hard as I'm paid to.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Lil_m01: <BLN>I'm not imagining it, right?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Lys_m01_001: I always had my fair share of women interested in\nme, even back in Saramis.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Lys_m01_002: And it seems the same is true here. I won't want for\ndining companions, to say the least.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Lys_m01: <BLN>It's the same all over.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sci_m01_001: How long has it been since I last set foot in the\ncapital? For so long I've swept across the continent...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sci_m01_002: In any case, with the Heroic Games beginning,\nthere are many more people here than my last visit.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sci_m01_003: Which means there are many more beauties for me\nto meet. The anticipation, it stirs me!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Sci_m01: <BLN>Look at all of them!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Moo_m01_001: I never thought I'd get to join such a big tournament.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Moo_m01_002: But since I am, I'm gonna give it all I got! And I\nwon't be sloppy!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Moo_m01: <BLN>Gonna give it my all!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Mic_m01_001: I haven't been here in a while, but Dagsion\nnever changes.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Mic_m01_002: Everyone is carefree and the city is lively, which is\ngood. What's not good is the crime, and the brawls.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Mic_m01_003: I bet parents raising their kids here never stop\nworrying. *sigh*
MID_LGA_1_M03_Mic_m01: <BLN>It's been a while!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Oly_m01_001: Ohoho! After thoroughly looking around, I can say\nthe capital has changed little since the old days.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Oly_m01_002: I, on the other hand, have changed. And in the\nHeroic Games I will dazzle and delight!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Oly_m01_003: All will behold the strength and beauty of the Blue\nRose of Caelus, Olympia Iris!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Oly_m01: <BLN>I will perform brilliantly.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Naz_m01_001: The Heroic Games have finally started!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Naz_m01_002: Woo! There's no time to sit around! I'm gonna go\ngrab a bite to eat and get back to my training!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Naz_m01: <BLN>There's no time to sit around!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sar_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sar_Dai_m01_001: What's with that flower behind your ear? I've never\nseen anything like that blooming in the village.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sar_Dai_m01_002: Oh, it's artificial. Lian Ren gave it to me to celebrate\nmy becoming a guardian.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sar_Dai_m01_003: What? That's no fair! Nobody gave me anything!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sar_Dai_m01_004: How could they? You didn't tell anyone you were\nleaving. You just up and decided to tag along.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Sar_m01: <BLN>It was a gift.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Dai_m01: <BLN>What's with that flower?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Hal_m01_001: The Heroic Games make me nervous. There's going\nto be scary-looking people, and I gotta fight them.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Hal_m01_002: B-but I need to remember that Nasshim taught me\nhow to fight! 
MID_LGV_1_M03_Hal_m01_003: I'll use my skills and be useful to everyone! I've just\ngotta give it all I got!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Hal_m01: <BLN>I've gotta give it all I got!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Guj_m01_001: So many hopefuls here for the games... Good for\nthem. I'd like to raise a toast to 'em all.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Guj_m01_002: Most everyone's probably feeling like they've got a\ngood shot at glory. Well, for now, you know?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Guj_m01_003: Later on, I don't think I'll like seeing all the unhappy\nfaces. So, let's enjoy this mood while it lasts!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Guj_m01: <BLN>I need a drink...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Yan_m01_001: So, the temples hope to awaken Dagda the Great\nwith these games... Could this actually work?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Yan_m01_002: And they insist that this will bring prosperity to\nthe people? What folly and pride!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Yan_m01: <BLN>What folly and pride!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Iio_m01_001: Rocinan may seem old, but I consider him a seasoned\npartner. He tips me off to danger with an ear twitch.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Iio_m01_002: He's a trusty steed, never stopping in his tracks,\nuntil I require us to hold up awhile.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Iio_m01_003: He just presses forward, trusting my judgment, and\nseems to value my direction.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Iio_m01: <BLN>My trusty steed...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Pep_m01_001: We ourselves can see Lady Ultand is forever busy\nwith the games. Should not others be helping more?!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Pep_m01_002: But we do wonder if the truth is that she's guiding\nmany others who are hard at work.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Pep_m01_003: Lady Ultand's nobility of character casts its light to\nand fro. As it did when she once graced us with aid!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Pep_m01: <BLN>We are almost offended!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Noc_m01_001: It's the talk of the city—the little guy who took\ndown the giant of the arena!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Noc_m01_002: What a story! And I heard that the big brute\nreally gave it his all too!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Noc_m01: <BLN>Everyone's talking about it...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sop_m01_001: I can't help but feel awed, thinking about all the gods\ngathered together.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sop_m01_002: Lord Solel was especially wonderful. That speech\nhe gave—so dramatic! He's the best of them all.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Sop_m01_003: I might be partial, working in his temple. I bet those\nwho work in the other temples feel the same.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Sop_m01: <BLN>How wonderful!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Cat_m01_001: Of all those here for the Heroic Games, who will\nbe the most promising employer?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Cat_m01_002: The strongest possibility is Queen Theodora. She\nputs her kingdom and people before all else.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Cat_m01_003: That risks being a little too narrow of purpose.\nStill, I wish more rulers were of like mind.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Cat_m01_004: Oh my! Queen Theodora! Y-you didn't happen to\nhear me musing aloud, did you?
MID_LGV_1_M03_Cat_m01_005: Well, I'm sure my earlier assessment of you will\nprove correct, Queen Theodora.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Cat_m01_006: Of course, I believe that I've already found the best\nemployer for me personally! Truly sterling!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Cat_m01: <BLN>If I had to choose...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Ned_m01_001: {SetColor=Gray}The queen of Saramis had so many retainers in her\ngrand procession... I saw some familiar faces...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_1_M03_Ned_m01_002: Sorry, I was lost in thought about my life before I\nbecame a mercenary. Old times, old comrades...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Ned_m01_003: Oh, Queen Theodora! I didn't realize it was you!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Ned_m01: <BLN>The Saramis procession...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Zac_m01_001: Can't stand those brats getting all the glory!\nI hate 'em.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Zac_m01_002: No respect for their elders. They should know their\ndamned place.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Zac_m01: <BLN>Those damn brats!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Maj_m01_001: It's STUPID that I can't be in the games! You can't\nhave a good games without the great Majide!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Maj_m01_002: This won't be the last people hear of me though!\nI'm a big deal—the BIGGEST!
MID_LGA_1_M03_Maj_m01: <BLN>It's so STUPID!
MID_LGV_1_M03_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Cen_m01_001: It's lamentable that Aurora wasn't able to ascend to\nher place amongst the gods at the colosseum.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Cen_m01_002: Forgive me... These are not the kind of things one\nwho serves the temples should say aloud.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Cen_m01: <BLN>I understand why, but still...
MID_LGV_1_M03_Gab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Gab_m01_001: A huge competition. The kind that hasn't happened\nfor centuries. How great.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Gab_m01_002: Great for ME, that is! Something like this happens,\neveryone's purse strings get reaaal loose.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Gab_m01_003: Hehehe. I'll have to be on my best behavior with the\ntemples for a while.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Gab_m01: <BLN>What a thing.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Lin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_Lin_m01_001: There's more of a racket lately. I take it the games\nhave started.
MID_LGV_1_M03_Lin_m01_002: When you're cooped up in a cell, you get to be\nsensitive to changes in the outside world.
MID_LGA_1_M03_Lin_m01: <BLN>So the games have started...
MID_LGV_1_M03_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B01_m01_001: Y'know, my grandpa said some of our ancestors\nhelped build the arena.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B01_m01_002: I mean, they only carried some stones around.\nIt didn't sound like a big, fancy job.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B01_m01_003: But Grandpa's real proud. He says, "We proved our\nworth to Lord Solel."
MID_LGA_1_M03_B01_m01: <BLN>Those were my ancestors...
MID_LGV_1_M03_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B02_m01_001: I happened to pass through a thick forest on my way\nhere to the capital.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B02_m01_002: My heart pounded with every step as I wondered if\nI'd run afoul of the Har Hali.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B02_m01_003: I've heard stories about folks who wandered into\ntheir territory and lost their heads. Brrr...
MID_LGA_1_M03_B02_m01: <BLN>How terrifying!
MID_LGV_1_M03_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B03_m01_001: It was worth coming to the match just to look upon\nthe exalted faces of the gods.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B03_m01_002: The whole time the bout was going on, I found\nmyself looking at the luxury seats instead of the fight.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B03_m01: <BLN>It was worth coming to the arena.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B04_m01_001: I'm good with horses and pegasi and the like, but I\nstill get nervous looking after war elephants.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B04_m01_002: I mean, have you seen the size of them? I worry I'll\nget crushed underfoot.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B04_m01: <BLN>Horses are one thing, but...
MID_LGV_1_M03_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B05_m01_001: Next time, I'm getting Mom to teach me how to\nmake honey-poached pears!
MID_LGV_1_M03_B05_m01_002: Our homemade ones are a little different. They're\nreal sweet and delicious! I bet you want one, huh?
MID_LGA_1_M03_B05_m01: <BLN>Doesn't it sound good?
MID_LGV_1_M03_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B06_m01_001: Being stuck with grunt work is the pits. I gotta get\nmyself promoted to decurion as fast as I can.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B06_m01_002: Then eventually, I'll be a centurion, then a pilus\nprior...and if I play my cards right, a commander!
MID_LGA_1_M03_B06_m01: <BLN>Someday...
MID_LGV_1_M03_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B07_m01_001: It was good to receive some votive offerings from\nregional viceroys for the opening ceremony.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B07_m01_002: But every one of them was absurdly ostentatious.\nThey're more interested in spectacle than devotion.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B07_m01: <BLN>Rather unsubtle of them.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B08_m01_001: I heard that Kalla, the Patron-Huntress, had a\npassionate affair with a mortal man long ago.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B08_m01_002: How marvelous must he have been to be loved by\na goddess?
MID_LGA_1_M03_B08_m01: <BLN>Have you heard this one?
MID_LGV_1_M03_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B09_m01_001: Tourists see the well-tended thermae and stalls and\nthink they know the city inside out.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B09_m01_002: But if you ask me, that's only one side of the\ncapital—the one the higher-ups want to be seen.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B09_m01: <BLN>If you ask me...
MID_LGV_1_M03_B10_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B10_m01_001: I came all the way to Dagsion and the best I could do\nfor lodgings was a run-down inn.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B10_m01_002: I thought I saved up a bundle out in the countryside,\nbut everything in the city is so expensive...
MID_LGA_1_M03_B10_m01: <BLN>These prices are outrageous!
MID_LGV_1_M03_B11_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B11_m01_001: Damn it, I lost my bet again. I thought maybe I could\nleave behind the pauper's life, but no.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B11_m01_002: Whatever. It's just my fate to live out my days here.\nI guess that's what the gods have in mind for me...
MID_LGA_1_M03_B11_m01: <BLN>It can only be fate...
MID_LGV_1_M03_B12_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B12_m01_001: The Heroic Games will be going on for quite a while,\nright? My little one's thrilled with all the excitement.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B12_m01_002: I expect he'll get bored after a few months, but for\nnow it's easiest to humor him.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B12_m01: <BLN>I'm glad he's pleased, but...
MID_LGV_1_M03_B13_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B13_m01_001: "I scraped the bottom of the lake." "The wood's rotted\nthrough." "We hit a cliff and broke the prow."
MID_LGV_1_M03_B13_m01_002: The excuses—and the repairs—never end. I'm\nswamped, but it's better than being idle.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B13_m01: <BLN>Plenty to do...
MID_LGV_1_M03_B14_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B14_m01_001: I managed to close a few deals with some retailers.\nBut my work isn't done yet!
MID_LGV_1_M03_B14_m01_002: I'm hoping to raise profits as quick as I can so the\nboss notices my potential.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B14_m01: <BLN>Can't rest on my laurels.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B15_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B15_m01_001: I really want to win my foreman's approval and\nbecome a fully fledged shipwright.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B15_m01_002: I dream of people setting sail for the other side of the\nworld aboard a ship I built...
MID_LGA_1_M03_B15_m01: <BLN>I need to get beyond apprenticing.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B16_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B16_m01_001: The strangest part of the imperial capital to me is\nthat people can actually fish in a bustling metropolis.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B16_m01_002: Lake Baal's waters are clean and its fish are a\ndelicacy. Fishing wound up becoming my hobby.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B16_m01_003: When you turn your back on the chaos of the city\nand gaze out on the water, you can find true peace.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B16_m01: <BLN>Fishing's great, ain't it?
MID_LGV_1_M03_B17_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B17_m01_001: It's the honor of a lifetime that I could come to the\ncapital as my queen's attendant.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B17_m01_002: I hope that my devotion to duty while stationed in\nthe capital will bring pride to my family.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B17_m01: <BLN>It's the honor of a lifetime!
MID_LGV_1_M03_B18_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B18_m01_001: I inherited this pot from my father. He'd heard it was\na masterpiece from Normalia.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B18_m01_002: But when I brought it to the Vandahl Trading\nCompany, they deemed it a counterfeit.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B18_m01_003: Their appraisals are very reliable. Sad to say, I think\nmy father was swindled.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B18_m01: <BLN>Sad to say, but...
MID_LGV_1_M03_B19_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B19_m01_001: Gah! No one's paying any attention to my\ncustom-built, king-sized, horse-drawn carriage!
MID_LGV_1_M03_B19_m01_002: All I get to hear about is the Saraminian procession.\nThose uncultured rabble!
MID_LGV_1_M03_B19_m01_003: What's so great about Saramis? A nation of filth who\nworships a goddess of death!
MID_LGA_1_M03_B19_m01: <BLN>What's so great about Saramis?!
MID_LGV_1_M03_B20_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B20_m01_001: I'm a sailor. Folks in my line of work come here to\npray quite a bit.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B20_m01_002: But there are those ugly rumors. Unless you have\nbusiness here, it might be better to stay away.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B20_m01: <BLN>Are the rumors true?
MID_LGV_1_M03_B21_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B21_m01_001: The kingdom of Saramis is situated at the\nsouthernmost point of Northern Dagda.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B21_m01_002: They perform the service of preventing barbarians\nfrom invading from the south.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B21_m01_003: That's why the temples recognize them as the\nShield of Dagda.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B21_m01: <BLN>We're all very grateful.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B22_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B22_m01_001: The land of Fódlan across the sea is a terribly\nbarbaric place, isn't it?
MID_LGV_1_M03_B22_m01_002: They have nations...of sorts...over there, but their\ngrip seems rather shaky.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B22_m01_003: Why, I hear that over half the continent is still under\nthe sway of barbarians.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B22_m01: <BLN>A sailor told me this once.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B23_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B23_m01_001: It seems some state visitors are staying in the\nguesthouses of Dagsion's hightown.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B23_m01_002: The royal family of Arago and that lot from Saramis\nwill be using them.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B23_m01_003: Security's probably pretty tight up there—regular folk\nwon't be able to get in.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B23_m01_004: After all, if anything happens to the bigwigs, it'll be\negg on the face of the Divine Sovereign.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B23_m01: <BLN>A soldier looked daggers at me!
MID_LGV_1_M03_B24_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B24_m01_001: I got so caught up in gambling that I frittered away\nevery last bit of my family's money.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B24_m01_002: Then, when my husband cottoned on, he kicked me\nout of the house. Oh, cruel fate!
MID_LGV_1_M03_B24_m01_003: I still enjoy gambling, though, and don't intend to\ngive it up. So I have a new plan.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B24_m01_004: I'll go and pray at Fortuna's temple! Who better to\npetition than the Goddess of Fate?
MID_LGA_1_M03_B24_m01: <BLN>I should pray.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B25_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B25_m01_001: All those gladiators are nothing more than\nne'er-do-wells who gamble their lives for a day's pay.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B25_m01_002: What do they offer the world, other than spectacle?\nIt's not a proper job.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B25_m01_003: Plenty of 'em are sidelined by injuries, assuming they\ndon't just up and die.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B25_m01_004: Though apparently some folk take up the lot of\na gladiator not for coin, but for kicks.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B25_m01: <BLN>It's not the life for me...
MID_LGV_1_M03_B26_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B26_m01_001: I, uh, heard you can get some excellent medicine\naround here.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B26_m01_002: By which I mean drams that bestow incredible\nstrength. That sort of thing.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B26_m01_003: If it's real, I'd like to snag a few vials and take them\nback to Fódlan for a tidy profit.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B26_m01: <BLN>Now where can I buy some?
MID_LGV_1_M03_B27_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B27_m01_001: I've lost count of how many times I've seen the\nWhite-Maned Demon fight.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B27_m01_002: But this is the first time I've seen him so outclassed\nthat he hit the dirt like that.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B27_m01: <BLN>That was a shock.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B28_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B28_m01_001: The Heroic Games are an unprecedented event in\nthe history of the Dagdan Empire.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B28_m01_002: Not only will the royal families of each nation be in\nattendance—so will the gods.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B28_m01_003: I only pray that the tournament will be aboveboard,\nwithout any unseemly incidents.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B28_m01: <BLN>Here's hoping for a safe event.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B29_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B29_m01_001: Have you ever encountered a pegasus? They're rare\nbeasts indeed.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B29_m01_002: Wing soldiers can soar through the sky on a winged\nhorse with ease, all while fighting.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B29_m01_003: It takes a special blend of riding skills and flying\nskills to make the cut as one.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B29_m01_004: Alas, those creatures only seem to take to women.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B29_m01: <BLN>Interested in being a wing soldier?
MID_LGV_1_M03_B30_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B30_m01_001: If it's strength that you seek, then you should undergo\ntraining to improve your skills.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B30_m01_002: It might seem tedious at first, but over time you'll\nstart to see results.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B30_m01: <BLN>There is no shortcut to mastery.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B31_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B31_m01_001: This land was once controlled by a nation called\nIskandariya.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B31_m01_002: Dagda the Great broke that control and claimed\ndominion over the land himself.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B31_m01_003: The legend of that clash has been passed down as\nthe Battle of Tarvos.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B31_m01: <BLN>An age long past...
MID_LGV_1_M03_B32_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B32_m01_001: There's supposedly a town called Da Mina\nsomewhere in this land.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B32_m01_002: Its people are said to be masterful crafters\nof weapons.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B32_m01_003: Should you ever get ahold of a weapon forged there,\nconsider yourself blessed.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B32_m01: <BLN>If I could merely gaze upon one...
MID_LGV_1_M03_B33_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B33_m01_001: You can visit the temples of all the divines who\ngovern this nation on Temple Row.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B33_m01_002: On the lower end are Credna's, Kalla's, Yu Phas's,\nand Aurora's temples.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B33_m01_003: While Jurah's, Solel's, Mars's, and Smyrnos's temples\nare found on the upper end.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B33_m01_004: Ascend the stairs to the top and you'll reach Dagda's\ntemple, where the Divine Sovereign holds court.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B33_m01: <BLN>There are many temples...
MID_LGV_1_M03_B34_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B34_m01_001: The nation on the southernmost tip of the empire,\nruled by Queen Theodora, is the kingdom of Saramis.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B34_m01_002: It's not yet been two centuries since its founding,\nmaking it the youngest of all the kingdoms of Dagda.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B34_m01_003: Though some would argue its continuity with\nDamascar makes it older than that.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B34_m01_004: The most noteworthy thing about Saramis is their\nfaith in Yu Phas, the Keeper of Death and Night.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B34_m01_005: In contrast to their devotion, most other parts of the\nDagdan Empire hold Yu Phas in contempt.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B34_m01: <BLN>Saramis is a young kingdom.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B35_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B35_m01_001: The gods who govern the land of Dagda are all of the\nDivine Emperor's pantheon.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B35_m01_002: Ah, no, not all. Yu Phas was not originally one\nof them.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B35_m01_003: She is from a different lineage, but became part of\nthe pantheon when she wed Lord Solel.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B35_m01: <BLN>This land is governed by gods.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B36_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B36_m01_001: Dagsion collects tributes from each of the counties in\nthe land of Dagda.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B36_m01_002: That makes it the wealthiest county of all.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B36_m01: <BLN>All tithes flow here.
MID_LGV_1_M03_B37_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1_M03_B37_m01_001: You shouldn't be here. Get lost.
MID_LGA_1_M03_B37_m01: <BLN>...